section CrPC CRPC Criminal Procedure Code Code of Criminal Procedure 201 CrPC section 201 The Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973 Procedure by Magistrate not competent to take cognizance of the case If the complaint is made to a Magistrate who is not competent to take cognizance of the offence, he shall,—
(a) if the complaint is in writing, return it for presentation to the proper Court with an endorsement to that effect;
(b) if the complaint is not in writing, direct the complainant to the proper Court.

